ings that are random um  the main thing that i do with with flash  carding and why i think it's so good is  aside from the fact that i'm i'm  reviewing some of these words and  phrases it also trains me to be more  attentive it makes me notice things  because when i do these flashcards i  also edit my captured phrases and i  review some of the case endings and i  become  quite you know it just develops that  ability to notice and if as i've said  many many times the key elements in  language learning are your attitude  including the confidence that you can  achieve it the time you spend on the  task and if you if you are able to do  the things that you like to do and focus  on doing things that you like to do  you're more likely to stay with it and  you're more likely to do it every day  and you're more likely to enjoy it  while you're doing it and of course the  third thing is this ability to notice  and i think random flash carding  is just as good for my ability to notice  as any effort that in my case would fail  to be systematic  uh in any kind of a spaced repetition  system  uh i made some notes here so i'm gonna  check uh to see uh yeah so believing is  very important and the biggest problem  that many classroom learners have is  that they don't  believe in anything really related to  their learning they're waiting every for  everything to come from the teacher  and so uh i believe that um  you know the other problem you know all  kinds of systems for example in the  classroom the teacher wants to teach a  certain grammar point and you must learn  it now so this i think to my mind  there's a that wants to resist all of  these systems spaced repetition systems  you've got to learn the grammar now  you've got to learn these words now they  should stick now the words kind of have  a  and any rule of grammar they all have a  mind of their own  which i think is quite random  and i don't believe that that you can  nail that down i don't believe in some  of the othe